  ---
  Why PostgreSQL Hasn't Merged posix_aio Yet

  From Thomas Munro's analysis (wiki + mailing lists):
  1. Worker mode is "good enough" - portable, works everywhere
  2. FreeBSD UFS limitations - no MNTK_SHARED_WRITES, no cache flush on fsync
  3. macOS AIO limits - restrictive limits make it less useful
  4. Focus on io_uring - that's where the performance gains are on Linux

  The posix_aio backend exists in development branches but hasn't been prioritized for merge.

  ---
  Key PostgreSQL Design Decisions Relevant to Your Port

  1. Completion callbacks run in critical sections (aio_internal.h:345-347) - can't ERROR out
  2. Any backend can complete any IO - needed for deadlock prevention
  3. AIO handles are recycled immediately - use PgAioWaitRef for waiting
  4. State machine is strictly ordered (IDLE → HANDED_OUT → DEFINED → STAGED → SUBMITTED → COMPLETED_*)

  Your TigerBeetle implementation follows a similar pattern with Completion structs and the aio_pending queue.

